.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH powerlinux-pick-color 1  "PowerLinux 0.1.0" "PowerLinux Manual"
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
powerlinux\-pick\-color \- Pick a color from the screen and copy its HEX value
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpowerlinux pick\-color\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
Pick a color from the screen and copy its HEX value
.PP
Uses the XDG Screenshot portal\*(Aqs color picker. The value is printed, copied to the clipboard and added to the color history shown in the control center.
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Pick a color and show all its formats:
.RS 4
.nf
\fBpowerlinux color "$(powerlinux pick\-color)"\fR
.fi
.RE
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBpowerlinux\fR(1)
